{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-budgeted-inference", "file": "references/session-138be90d-block-summary.md", "content": "# 3×3 block color summary: verified instance

A 15×15 noisy multicolor input mapped to a 5×5 output, suggesting non-overlapping 3×3 blocks aligned from the upper-left. The demo was 27×27→9×9, with the same 3×3 partition. In each block, count non-background cells by color (excluding background 5); the output cell is the most frequent non-background color, or 0 if the block contains no non-background color. The complete 9×9 demo output matched this summary, including zero-valued blocks. Applying the same rule to the test produced the accepted 5×5 output.

Important validation: output zero in this rule represents an empty-signal block, not a claim that raw input zero is the background. The noisy input contains raw zeros as well as colors 3, 6, 8, and 9. Do not substitute center sampling, any-color presence, or a generic block mode including background 5 without checking every block against the demo. Here tie cases did not interfere with the validated result. For analogous tasks, reconstruct the entire demo output first and check output-background semantics before submitting.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-seq0/frozen/seen/play/users/u025/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-budgeted-inference/references/session-138be90d-block-summary.md"}

