{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-demo-checkpoint", "file": "references/session-line-object-relation.md", "content": "# Divider-plus-object relational rule

This task's four demos look unlike one another locally, but each contains a full-length divider/marker line and a compact colored object on one side. The output preserves the input and adds a line parallel to the divider, on the object's side, at the object's far edge: the new line lies between the object and divider. Normalize orientations to compare: horizontal divider plus object above/below, or vertical divider plus object left/right. In the test, the full horizontal color-1 band is at row 6; the sparse color-3 object is above it, with its farthest extent at row 4, so the derived line would be row 5 (between object and band). This explains why recoloring the sparse motif or filling all background was erroneous.

Inference checklist: identify the continuous separator, establish the object side and its extent toward the separator, and infer a parallel continuation/border line between object and divider. Preserve the separator, object, and all unrelated cells. Validate direction, adjacency/offset, and color mapping against each current demo before applying; this is a task-specific synthesis, not a universal ARC rule.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-seq0/frozen/seen/play/users/u025/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-demo-checkpoint/references/session-line-object-relation.md"}

